From dab97a02f0c0881ea561ee723eac525f3c48549c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy1210 <andy1210@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:21:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 066/149] clk: qcom: camcc-sm8350: Use the shared RCG ops and
 the MX power domain

Measured on the Surface Duo 2: with plain clk_rcg2_ops (and the vendor's
HW clock control bit) CAMSS's first clk_set_rate on the IFE0 source of a
disabled RCG left it unswitched ("rcg didn't update its configuration"),
since its new parent PLL was not running. Use the shared RCG ops for every
source but the XO and sleep ones, as camcc-sm8250 does (the configuration
is parked while the RCG is off and applied when it is enabled), and drop
the HW clock control bit, as camcc-sm8250 and camcc-sm8450 do.

The vendor driver supplies the controller from both MMCX and MX (vdd_mm,
vdd_mx). Describe both power domains, as for SM8550, and probe through
qcom_cc_probe() so that both are attached and on before the PLLs are
configured (the driver's own runtime PM handling configured them before
a second domain could be attached).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
